hadiths[153]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4801","Another: 146 - Abu Jafar and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated: Milhan ibn Sulayman al-Dawraqi narrated: Abdullah ibn Dawud al-Khuraybi narrated: al-Amash narrated: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Ali and Fatimah while they were laughing, and when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) they fell silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What is with you, you were laughing, then when you saw me you fell silent? Fatimah hastened and said: May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! He said: I am more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you. So I said: Rather I am more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: O my daughter, you have the tenderness of a child, and Ali is dearer to me than you."
"4802","Another: 147 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym narrated: Misar narrated: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: He gave concession to an old man while fasting, and forbade a young man."
"4803","Another: 148 - With it Sulayman informed us: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated: Shubah informed us: from Abu Bishr: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: You shall surely ride stage upon stage. He said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4804","Another: 149 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Abbas al-Nasai al-Baghdadi narrated: Sahl ibn Ibrahim al-Marwazi narrated: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated: my father narrated to me: Abu Amr ibn al-Ala narrated: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Whatever is in the Quran as qattal - with shadda - is punishment, and whatever is qatal - without shadda - is mercy."
"4805","Another: 150 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated: Raja ibn al-Harith narrated: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of them are those easiest in dowry."
"4806","151 - Al-Tabarani said: Musa ibn Harun narrated: Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated: from Abu al-Harith - Ishaq ibn Rahawayh said: he is Raja - from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The best of them are those easiest in dowry. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah from Abu Ammar Husayn ibn Hurayth. Raja ibn al-Harith Abu Said al-Makki from Mujahid: Yahya ibn Main said: weak."
"4807","Another: 152 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Hadrami - he is Muhammad ibn Abdullah - narrated: Ibrahim ibn Abi Muawiyah narrated: my father narrated: from al-Amash: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: All flies are in the Fire except the bee. Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Khazim: Abu Zurah said: There is no harm in him, truthful."
"4808","Another: 153 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Narsi al-Baghdadi narrated: Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Muqri al-Duri narrated: Abu Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated: Abu Amr ibn al-Ala narrated to me: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: that he used to recite: It is not for a prophet to embezzle. And how can it be that he may not embezzle when he may be killed; Allah said: And they kill the prophets. But the hypocrites accused the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of something, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: It is not for a prophet to embezzle."
"4809","154 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja al-Hanbali al-Isbahani informed us, there: Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sanusi narrated: Ahmad ibn Faraj narrated: Hafs ibn Umar al-Muqri narrated: Yahya ibn al-Mubarak Abu Muhammad al-Yazidi narrated: from Abu Amr ibn al-Ala: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: How can it be that he may not embezzle when he could be killed; Allah said: And they kill the prophets without right. But the hypocrites accused the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Allah revealed: It is not for a prophet to embezzle."
"4810","Another: 155 - With it Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Muawiyah al-Kufi narrated: Abdullah ibn Kathir al-Amiri narrated: Muhammad ibn Junayd narrated: Musab ibn Sallam narrated: from Sad: from al-Hakam: from Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj: from Ibn Abbas, who said: I asked him about the end of Al Imran. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was late one night, then he prayed with the people. He said: He came out after a third of the night had passed and saw the mosque nearly empty. He said: Why do I not see the people? They said: You were late, O Messenger of Allah, upon the people, so they prayed. He said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would make it at this hour; none of the two People of the Book pray it except you. Then was revealed: O you who believe, be patient and persevere and remain stationed and fear Allah that you may succeed. He said: It was revealed about jihad."
"4811","Another: 156 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us: Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdan al-Saffar narrated: Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari narrated: Ali ibn Mansur narrated: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated: from Sufyan ibn Husayn: from al-Hakam: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas, who said: Marriage to women of the People of the Book is not lawful when they are at war. Then he recited this verse: Fight those who do not believe in Allah nor the Last Day, up to His saying: while they are humbled. Al-Hakam said: I narrated it to Ibrahim and it pleased him."
"4812","Another: 157 - With it Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Musaddad narrated: Fadl narrated: from Husayn: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas about His saying: And she prepared for them a cushion. He said: Citron."
"4813","158 - With it Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq narrated: Ishaq al-Harbi narrated: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated: Abu Kudaynah narrated: from Hafs: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas about: And she prepared for them a cushion and gave each one of them a knife. He said: She gave them citron and gave each one of them a knife, and when they saw Yusuf they extolled him and began cutting their hands while thinking they were cutting the citron."
"4814","Another: 159 - With it Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Kufi narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym: from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about the saying of Allah: And Allah presents an example of two men, one of them dumb, unable to do anything, the verse. Ibn Abbas said: It was revealed about Uthman ibn Affan and a freedman of Uthman who was a disbeliever, who was among Uthmans dependents; he called him to Islam and he refused, and Allah revealed: And Allah presents an example of two men, one of them dumb, unable to do anything, up to His saying: and he is on a straight path. He said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4815","Another: 160 - With it Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mardawayh informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated: Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir narrated: my father narrated: Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated: Ismail ibn al-Yasa narrated, he said: Umar ibn Dharr narrated to me, he said: Mujahid narrated to me: from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abdullah ibn Rawahah while he was reminding his companions, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed you are the assembly whom Allah commanded me to keep myself with. Then he recited this verse: And keep yourself with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His Face, up to: and his affair was excess. Indeed, whenever your number sits, their number of angels sits with them."
"4816","Another: 161 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khabbaz informed us, in Isbahan: Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated: Jafar al-Saigh narrated: Affan narrated: Wuhayb narrated: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated: from Mujahid, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas about His saying: Until when he reaches full strength. He said: About thirty-three years. Then he said: Did We not grant you life wherein whoever would remember could remember. He said: It is forty-six years, and it is the age by which Allah excuses the son of Adam."
"4817","Another: 162 - With it Ahmad ibn Musa informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated: Mihran ibn Harun narrated: Muhammad ibn Salih al-Sari narrated: Ishaq ibn al-Hajjaj narrated: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated: from Mihran: from Sufyan: from al-Amash: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: that he used to say about: They do not listen to the Exalted Assembly. He said: They used to eavesdrop but would not hear, and when was revealed: Indeed the tree of Zaqqum, food of the sinful, Abu Jahl called for dates and butter and said: Gorge yourselves. Then Allah revealed: Indeed it is a tree emerging at the root of Hell. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: And We frighten them, but it only increases them in great transgression. The Mihran who narrated from Sufyan is Ibn Abi Umar al-Razi al-Attar: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: trustworthy, righteous in hadith."
"4818","Another: 163 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muaddib informed us: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, recited to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Abu Amr narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated: Adam narrated: Hushaym narrated: from Abu Bishr: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas about His saying: The Day the Spirit stands. He said: The Spirit is a matter of Allahs command, a creation of Allahs creation; He formed them in the image of the sons of Adam, and no angel descends from heaven but with him is one of the Spirit."
"4819","Another: 164 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi informed us, in Isbahan: Said al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Hushaym narrated: Abu Bishr informed us: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas: that he said about: You shall surely ride stage upon stage. He said: Meaning your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: state after state. Shubah narrated it from Abu Bishr from Mujahid likewise."
"4820","Another: 165 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Dubayli narrated: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated: Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated: from Ibn Abi Najih: from Mujahid: from Ibn Abbas about His saying: And they withhold al-Maun. He said: Lending of goods, and Ali said: The obligatory zakah; they withhold their zakah. Its end, and praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace."
"4821","The sixty-ninth part of the Selected Hadiths. In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, and praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless him and grant peace abundantly. Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, whose name is Alqamah ibn Khalid ibn al-Harith ibn Abi Usayd ibn Rifah ibn Thalabah ibn Hawazin ibn Aslam ibn Afsa al-Aslami Abu Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him. Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Saksaki Abu Ismail al-Kufi from Abdullah. 166 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isbahan: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: al-Qawariri narrated: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated: Misar narrated: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained of forgetting the Quran. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. Then he came later and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, provide for me, and guide me. He said: He counted them on his hand. He said: And he closed his fingers. When he turned away the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for this one, he has filled his hand with good."
"4822","167 - With it Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated: Umar ibn Ali narrated: from Misar: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I do not know anything of the Quran, so teach me something that will suffice me from it. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. He said: This is for my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, provide for me, and grant me health."
"4823","168 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym narrated: Misar narrated: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I cannot take anything of the Quran, so teach me something that will suffice me from the Quran. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. He said: This is for Allah, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me. Misar said: And perhaps I asked some of it from Abu Khalid."
"4824","169 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated: from Abd al-Razzaq: from al-Thawri. Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nuaym narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Abu Khalid al-Wasiti: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I cannot learn the Quran, so what will suffice me? He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest. He said: The man said: Like this, and he joined his five fingers, and said: This is for Allah, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me health, guide me, and provide for me. He said: The man closed both his palms together, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for this one, he has filled his hands with good. Sufyan said: The reckoning of the Arabs was likewise. Al-Masudi Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Masud and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated it from Ibrahim. And Abu Usamah and Umar ibn Ali narrated it from Misar. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Nuaym. And from Waki from Sufyan from Yazid al-Dalani, and from Yazid ibn Harun from al-Masudi. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Waki from Sufyan from Abu Khalid Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dalani. And al-Nasai narrated it from Yusuf ibn Isa and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan from al-Fadl ibn Musa from Misar, and said: Ibrahim al-Saksaki is not that strong. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab from Ibrahim ibn Bashshar from Sufyan from Misar, up to his saying: and Allah is Greatest; Sufyan said: I think he said: and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. And he narrated it in full from Abu Yala al-Mawsili from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami from Umar ibn Ali from Misar. Muslim narrated from the narration of Musab ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from his father something similar."
"4825","Another: 170 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Fath ibn Makki al-Nahrawani informed us, in Baghdad: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Sallal al-Warraq informed them. And Abu Hamid Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit ibn Zayd informed us, in Baghdad, and Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib, in the outskirts of Damascus: Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Zawzani informed them, they said: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Wishah ibn Abdullah, freedman of the Zaynabiyin, informed us: Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Shahin narrated: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated, I asked him. And Shuja ibn Salim ibn Ali ibn Salamah al-Baytar informed us, in the western side of Baghdad: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Dallal informed them, recited to him while he was present: al-Khatib Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarifini informed us: Abu al-Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis narrated, dictation: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated, from his wording. 171 - And Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us, in the outskirts of Damascus: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by ijazah. And Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed them, recited to him in Baghdad: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Asim narrated, they said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala narrated: Sufyan - he is Ibn Uyaynah - narrated: from Misar: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of Allahs servants are those who watch the sun and the moon and the shadows for the remembrance of Allah. In the narration of Ibn Said: Indeed the best of Allahs servants. Ibn Shahin said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah is alone in it from Misar; none narrated it from him but he, and it is a strange, sound, good hadith; Yahya ibn Abi Bakr al-Kirmani narrated it from Ibn Uyaynah. And Abu Nuaym said: Sufyan is alone from Misar in raising it. And Khallad and others narrated it from Misar as mawquf."
"4826","172 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyah informed us: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Misar: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the best of Allahs servants are those who watch the sun and the moon and the stars for the remembrance of Allah."
"4827","Another: 173 - Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by ijazah. And Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzali informed them, in Baghdad, recited to him: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, they said: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Hafiz narrated: Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Abbas al-Bazzaz narrated, in Antioch: Uthman ibn Khurrazadh narrated: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Misar: from Ibrahim al-Saksaki: from Ibn Abi Awfa: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the shadows lengthen and the winds blow, raise your needs to Allah; for it is the hour of the oft-returning; indeed He is Forgiving, Merciful to the oft-returning. Abu Nuaym said: Strange from the hadith of Misar; we wrote it only from him. Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Saksaki: Shubah criticized him and said: He did not speak well. Al-Bukhari narrated for him in his Sahih a hadith from the narration of Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: that a man stood a while in the market and swore he had been offered for it what he had not been offered, to entrap a Muslim man therein, so this verse was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with Allahs covenant and their oaths a small price."
"4828","Ismail ibn Abi Khalid al-Kufi from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 174 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Isbahani narrated: al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Rukhami narrated: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated: Isa ibn Yunus narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I hope that no man who crossed al-Aqabah will enter the Fire."
"4829","Another: 175 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nizak narrated: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid: from Ibn Abi Awfa: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A mans spending on his family is charity."
"4830","Another: 176 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a funeral, and he said takbir over it four times."
"4831","Al-Hakam ibn Utaybah al-Kufi from Ibn Abi Awfa. 177 - Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi and others informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Abdullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Shubah narrated: al-Hakam ibn Utaybah informed us: from Ibn Abi Awfa: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a plunder of high value while he is a believer. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Said ibn al-Musayyib, Abu Salamah, and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah."
"4832","Ziyad ibn Fayyad al-Khuzai Abu al-Hasan al-Kufi from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 178 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us. And Abu Jafar and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, they said: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated - al-Tabarani said: Ibn Harun - Misar informed us: from Ziyad ibn Fayyad: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, to You is praise, abundant, good, blessed therein. In al-Tabaranis narration from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4833","Said ibn Jumhan al-Aslami al-Basri from Ibn Abi Awfa. 179 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Bahz and Affan narrated, the meaning, they said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated. Affan said in his hadith: Said ibn Jumhan narrated, and Bahz said in his hadith: Said ibn Jumhan narrated to me, he said: We were with Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa fighting the Khawarij, and a slave boy of Ibn Abi Awfa had joined the Khawarij, so we called him: O Fayruz! This is Ibn Abi Awfa. He said: What a good man, if only he would emigrate. He said: What does the enemy of Allah say? He said: He says: What a good man, if only he would emigrate. He said: Emigration after my emigration with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), repeating it three times. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Blessed is he who kills them and then they kill him. Affan said in his hadith: and they kill him, three times."
"4834","180 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Baghdadi narrated: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: Said ibn Jumhan narrated, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa said to me: What happened to your father? I said: The Azariqah killed him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Dogs of the Fire, the worst slain under the shade of the sky; blessed is he who kills them; blessed is your father."
"4835","181 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated, he said: Said ibn Jumhan narrated to me, he said: I met Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa while he was blind, so I greeted him. He said to me: Who are you? I said: I am Said ibn Jumhan. He said: What happened to your father? I said: The Azariqah killed him. He said: May Allah curse the Azariqah, may Allah curse the Azariqah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that they are the dogs of the Fire. He said: I said: The Azariqah alone or all the Khawarij? He said: Rather all the Khawarij. He said: I said: The ruler wrongs the people and does to them and does to them. He said: He took my hand and squeezed it hard, and said: Woe to you, O Ibn Jumhan, hold to the great multitude; if the ruler will listen to you, go to him in his house and tell him what you know; if he accepts from you, well, otherwise leave him, for you are not more knowledgeable than he. Said ibn Jumhan was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Main, and Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not used as proof, without explaining the criticism, and this phrase is repeated from Abu Hatim about more than one of the men of the Sahih."
"4836","Sufyan ibn al-Mukhtar, and it is said Ibn Abi Habibah, Abu al-Mukhtar al-Asadi, from Ibn Abi Awfa. 182 - Abu al-Ghanayim Shirawayh ibn Shahrazad ibn Shirawayh al-Daylami informed us, in Hamadhan, and Abu Mahmud Asad ibn Hamad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi, and Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah, and Abu Shuja Ridwan ibn Muhammad ibn Mahfuz ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Thaqafi, and Abu Ismail Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Mashadhah, and Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi, all together, in Isbahan, and Abu al-Muzaffar Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Munim ibn Mashadhah, in Shahrastan: Abu al-Qasim Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, recited to him while they listened: al-Ustadh Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Sabuni informed us: Abu Said Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Razi informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Yahya ibn Durays al-Razi al-Bajali informed us: Abu Amr Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us, Shubah said: from Abu al-Mukhtar: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who serves drink to the people is the last of them to drink."
"4837","183 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym narrated: Shubah narrated: from Abu al-Mukhtar, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The one who serves drink to the people is the last of them."
"4838","184 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad - he is Ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami - Yahya al-Qattan narrated: from Shubah, he said: Abu al-Mukhtar narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who serves drink to the people is the last of them."
"4839","185 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Hajjaj narrated: Shubah narrated to me: from Abu al-Mukhtar, of Banu Asad, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: We were on a journey and could not find water. He said: Then we came upon water later. He said: They began giving the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink, and whenever they brought him drink, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who serves drink to the people is the last of them, three times, until they all drank. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Muhammad ibn Jafar from Shubah. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Abdullah ibn Rabah from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari."
"4840","Sulayman ibn Fayruz al-Shaybani Abu Ishaq al-Kufi from Ibn Abi Awfa. 186 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated: Amr ibn Asim narrated: Imran Abu al-Awwam narrated: from al-Shaybani: from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is with the judge so long as he does not commit injustice."
"4841","187 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated: Amr ibn Asim narrated: Abu al-Awwam narrated: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is with the judge so long as he does not commit injustice; if he commits injustice, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, disassociates from him and Satan clings to him. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar from Amr ibn Asim. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Qattan from Muhammad ibn Bilal from Imran. And al-Tirmidhi said: A strange hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Imran. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili. Abu al-Awwam Imran ibn Dawar al-Qattan: some criticized him, and some praised him, and Allah knows best."
"4842","Shatha al-Kufiyah from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 188 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Said al-Qawariri narrated, he is Ubayd Allah ibn Umar: Salamah ibn Raja al-Kufi narrated: Shatha narrated to us, she said: I saw Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa pray Duha two rakahs, and his wife said to him: You prayed only two rakahs. He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Duha two rakahs when he was given glad tidings of the conquest and of the head of Abu Jahl."
"4843","189 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym and Mualla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated. Al-Tabarani said: And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Rawh ibn Abd al-Mumin al-Muqri narrated. He said: And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, they said: Salamah ibn Raja narrated: Shatha narrated to us: that Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa prayed Duha two rakahs, and his wife said to him: You prayed it only two rakahs. He said: Indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rakahs on the day of the conquest."
"4844","190 - Abu Shuja Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Maqrun al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khayyat informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn informed us: Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated: Salt ibn Masud narrated: Salamah ibn Raja narrated: Shatha narrated to us, she said: I saw Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa pray Duha two rakahs, and the mother of his child said to him: You prayed it only two rakahs. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Duha two rakahs on the day of the conquest of Makkah and the day he was given glad tidings of the head of Abu Jahl. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf from Maslamah in the mention of the head of Abu Jahl. Salamah ibn Raja: some declared him trustworthy and some criticized him. And al-Bukhari narrated for him."
"4845","Talhah ibn Musarrif from Ibn Abi Awfa. 191 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Awanah Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Naysaburi narrated: Abu Umayyah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated: al-Fadl ibn Muwaffaq narrated: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated: from Talhah ibn Musarrif: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I cannot learn the Quran, so teach me what will suffice me from the Quran. He said: Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. He said: This is for Allah, so what is for me? He said: Say: Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me health, and provide for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has filled his hands with good. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Isbahani from Abu Umayyah."
"4846","Abdullah ibn Said from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 192 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad narrated: Iyad narrated: from Abdullah ibn Said: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A distant man came while we were in the row behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he entered the row, then said: Allah is Greatest, greatly, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. The Muslims raised their heads and disapproved of the man, and said: Who is raising his voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who is this loud-voiced one? It was said: This one, O Messenger of Allah! He said: By Allah, I saw your speech ascend to heaven until a door of it opened and it entered through it. 193 - With it my father narrated to me: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated: Iyad narrated: from Abdullah ibn Said: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa."
"4847","194 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Darran ibn Sufyan al-Qattan al-Basri and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated. Al-Tabarani said: And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated, they said: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated, meaning Iyad narrated: from Abdullah ibn Said: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A man came while we were in prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Allah is Greatest, greatly, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. The Muslims raised their heads and disapproved of his voice. And they said: Who is this who raises his voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed the prayer, he said: Who is this loud-voiced one? They said: It is this one, O Messenger of Allah! He said: By Allah, I saw your speech ascend in the sky until a door was opened for it and it entered. The wording is al-Tabaranis narration. And in Imam Ahmads narration: A man came while we were in the row behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered the row. He said: And with him: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who is this loud-voiced one? It was said: Here he is. And at its end: and it entered it."
"4848","195 - Abu Jafar Muhammad informed us, also: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Qabbab informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad narrated: from Abdullah ibn Said: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: A distant man came while we were in prayer and entered the row, and said: Allah is Greatest, greatly, and praise be to Allah abundantly, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. The Muslims raised their heads and disapproved of the man. And they said: Who is this who raised his voice above the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who is this loud-voiced one? It was said: Here he is. He said: By Allah, I saw his speech ascend in the sky until a door of it was opened and it entered it."
"4849","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr ibn Suwayd al-Kufi from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 196 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Hamad al-Saigh informed us, in Isbahan: Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshidh narrated, his saying: al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Abi Madhur narrated: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shubah informed us: from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, who said: I entered upon Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, I and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and we asked him about the Greater Hajj. He said: It is the day of Nahr; it is the day of blood."
"4850","Awwam ibn Hawshab ibn Yazid ibn Ruwaym al-Shaybani Abu Isa al-Wasiti from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 197 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated: from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The najish is a consumer of usury, cursed."
"4851","Amir ibn Sharahil al-Shabi from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 198 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf complained of Khalid ibn al-Walid to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Khalid, why do you harm a man of the people of Badr? If you spent the like of Uhud in gold you would not reach his deed. He said: O Messenger of Allah, they attack me so I reply to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, which Allah poured upon the disbelievers."
"4852","199 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated: al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated: from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid: from al-Shabi: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf complained of Khalid ibn al-Walid to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Khalid, why do you harm a man of the people of Badr? If you spent the like of Uhud in gold you would not reach his deed. He said: They attack me so I reply to them. He said: Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah, which He poured upon the disbelievers. Abu Ismail al-Muaddib: his name is Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Muaddib: in one narration from Yahya ibn Main: he is weak, and in a narration from him and from Imam Ahmad: there is no harm in him."
"4853","Al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Ibn Abi Awfa. 200 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ismail narrated: Ayyub narrated: from al-Qasim al-Shaybani: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: Muadh came to Yemen - or he said: al-Sham - and saw the Christians prostrating to their patriarchs or bishops, so he conceived in himself that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more deserving to be honored. When he came, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw the Christians prostrating to their patriarchs and bishops, so I conceived in myself that you are more deserving to be honored. He said: If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the wife to prostrate to her husband, and the wife does not fulfill all of Allahs right upon her until she fulfills all of her husbands right. Even if he asks her for herself while she is on the back of a saddle, she should give it to him."
"4854","201 - Abu al-Karam Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Sami ibn Muhammad al-Abbasi informed us, in Baghdad: Abu al-Qasim Hibah Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Hariri informed them, he said: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Barmali narrated: Abu al-Husayn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Jafar ibn Bayan informed us: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mustafad al-Firyabi narrated: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Ayyub: from al-Qasim al-Shaybani: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: When Muadh came to Yemen, he prostrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw them prostrating, so I conceived in myself to prostrate to you when I saw you. He said: Do not do it; for if I were to command anyone to prostrate to other than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, I would command the wife to prostrate to her husband, and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, she does not fulfill her Lords right, Mighty and Majestic, until she fulfills her husbands right. Even if he asks her for herself upon a saddle, she must not refuse him. Ibn Majah narrated it from Azhar ibn Marwan from Hammad ibn Zayd similarly."
"4855","Al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Wazzan from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 202 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Darran al-Qattan al-Basri narrated: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated: al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Wazzan narrated, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa in the market among the money-changers, and he said: O company of money-changers, rejoice. They said: May Allah give you glad tidings of Paradise; with what do you give us glad tidings, O Abu Muhammad? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rejoice of the Fire."
"4856","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah al-Ansari from Ibn Abi Awfa. 203 - Abu Jafar and Fatimah informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Isbahani narrated: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Sufi narrated: Muhammad ibn Uqbah - brother of al-Walid ibn Uqbah - narrated: from Abu Ishaq: from Shubah: from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah: from Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hears the call on Friday and does not come to it, then hears the call and does not come to it, three times, Allah seals his heart and makes it the heart of a hypocrite."
"4857","Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid al-Kufi from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 204 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Hushaym narrated: al-Shaybani informed us: from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, who said: The people of the mosque sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa to ask him what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did with the food of Khaybar. So I came to him and asked him about that. He said: And I said: Did he take a fifth of it? He said: No, it was less than that. He said: When one of us wanted something of it, he took what he needed of it."
"4858","205 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Hushaym narrated: al-Shaybani and Ashath informed us: from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, who said: The people of the mosque sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa to ask him what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did with the food of Khaybar. He said: So I came to him and asked him about that. He said: I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a fifth of it? He said: No, it was less than that. And when one of us wanted something of it, he took what he needed of it. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Kurayb from Abu Muawiyah from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani."
"4859","Mudrik ibn Umarah ibn Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt al-Qurashi from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 206 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated: Shubah narrated: from Firas: from Mudrik ibn Umarah: from Ibn Abi Awfa: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor steal while he is a believer, nor plunder a plunder of high value or lavishness while plundering it while he is a believer."
"4860","207 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya - he is Ibn Said - narrated: Shubah narrated: from Firas: from Mudrik ibn Umarah: from Ibn Abi Awfa: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He does not drink wine while drinking it while he is a believer, nor does the adulterer commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a plunder of high value or lavishness while he is a believer. This hadith has already come in the narration of al-Hakam ibn Utaybah from the narration of Ahmad ibn Mani. And Ibn Mani narrated after it from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Shubah from Firas, he said: I heard Mudrik ibn Umarah: that he heard Ibn Abi Awfa narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise."
"4861","Yahya ibn Uqayl al-Khuzai al-Basri from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. 208 - Abu al-Qasim Hibah Allah ibn Ali al-Busiri informed us, in al-Fustat: Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini al-Muaddal informed them, recited to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn, known as Ibn al-Tifl, informed us, recited to him: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariya ibn Hayyawayh informed us, recited to him: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasai narrated: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Ghazwan - he is Ibn Abi Rizmah - informed us: al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us: from al-Husayn ibn Waqid: Yahya ibn Uqayl narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah much, engage little in idle talk, lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon, and would not disdain to walk with the widow and the poor to fulfill their need. Thus al-Nasai narrated it in his book."
"4862","209 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nuqur informed us, he said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, recited to him while I listened, it was said to him: Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Abdullah ibn Mayyah al-Hadrami narrated to you: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated: from al-Husayn ibn Waqid: from Yahya ibn Uqayl, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to remember Allah much, engage little in idle talk, lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon, and would neither disdain nor be too proud to walk with the widow and the poor until he fulfilled their need. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah from Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth. And from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi from Ishaq from al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"4863","Another: 210 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Tabarzad informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, recited to him: the two shaykhs Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Nuqur and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Aziz ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati informed us, they said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us: Abdullah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated: Luwayn narrated: Ismail ibn Zakariya narrated: from Muhammad ibn Awn: from Yahya ibn Uqayl al-Khuzai: from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith before it. He said: The destroyers are three: a mans admiration of himself, stinginess obeyed, and misleading desire."
"4864","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Adawi Abu Abd al-Rahman, may Allah be pleased with him. Adam ibn Ali al-Ijli al-Shaybani from Abdullah ibn Umar. 211 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jahm al-Samari narrated, they said: Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated: Abu Dawud narrated: Shubah narrated: from Adam ibn Ali: he heard Ibn Umar. [The matn is absent in the source row; the chain ends here.]"
"4865","212 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isbahan: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Jahm narrated: Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated: Shubah narrated: from Adam ibn Ali: that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fruit is not to be sold until it ripens. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Shubah but Abu Dawud; Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman is alone in it."
"4866","Another: 213 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim al-Zuhri narrated: my uncle narrated: my father narrated: from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Misar ibn Kidam al-Hilali narrated to me: from Adam ibn Ali al-Bakri: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not spread your arms as the beast spreads, and press upon your palms, and keep away from your sides; for when you do that, every limb of you prostrates. Thus Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih."
"4867","214 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us of it: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated: Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated: my father and my uncle narrated: from their father: from Ibn Ishaq: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to me: from Adam ibn Ali: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spread your arms as the beast spreads, and press upon your palms, and keep your elbows away from your sides. And Abdullah and Ubayd Allah, sons of Sad ibn Ibrahim, narrate from their father and their uncle. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Abdullah ibn Sad similarly."
"4868","Another: 215 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us: Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated: Abu Bakr al-Talhi narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated: Ismail ibn Abi al-Hakam - he was trustworthy - narrated: Yahya ibn Yaman narrated: from Sufyan al-Thawri: from Adam ibn Ali: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to a man on the Day of Resurrection: Stand and intercede, so he will intercede for his tribe; then it will be said to another: Stand and intercede, so he will intercede for the household; then it will be said to another: Stand and intercede, so he will intercede for a man and two men according to his deed. Ahmad ibn Abdullah said: Strange from the hadith of Adam; none narrated it from him but al-Thawri."
"4869","216 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us of it: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by ijazah: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us with its chain likewise. Al-Bukhari narrated from Ismail ibn Aban from Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym from Adam ibn Ali from Ibn Umar, saying: The people will become on the Day of Resurrection in heaps; every nation following its prophet. They will say: O so-and-so, intercede for us, until intercession ends at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); that is al-Maqam al-Mahmud. And in what we mentioned is what he did not mention."
"4870","Aslam Abu Khalid, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abdullah ibn Umar. 217 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu Zuraah Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them, in Baghdad: Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Muqawwimi informed us: Abu Talhah al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah ibn Bahr al-Qattan informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from his father: from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Fara and no Atirah. Thus Ibn Majah brought it out."
"4871","Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhuayb al-Madani al-Qurashi from Ibn Umar. 218 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Ibn Abi Najih: from Ismail ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhuayb, who said: We went out with Ibn Umar and the sun set, and we were awed of Ibn Umar to say to him: The prayer. He waited until the whiteness of the horizon and the darkness of Isha had gone, then alighted and prayed three rakahs, then led us in two rakahs, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim from Sufyan similarly. And al-Bukhari narrated, from the narration of Aslam, freedman of Umar, who said: I was with Ibn Umar on the road to Makkah when news reached him of Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd's severe pain, and he mentioned the hadith, and at its end he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, delay Maghrib and combine them."
"4872","Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid from Abdullah ibn Umar. 219 - Abu al-Qasim Said ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Attaf al-Mawsili informed us, in Baghdad: Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarifini informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Khalaf ibn Zunbur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Dawud informed us: Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Salih narrated: Anbasah narrated: Yunus narrated: from Ibn Shihab: that Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him: that Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid informed him: that he asked Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we find the prayer of residence and the prayer of fear, so tell me about the prayer of travel, for we do not find that in the Quran. Ibn Umar said: O son of my brother, indeed Allah, exalted His praise, sent to us Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we knew nothing, so we only do as we saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"4873","220 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, in Isbahan: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated: Yunus informed me: from Ibn Shihab: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me: from Umayyah ibn Khalid ibn Asid: that he asked Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I said to him: What about shortening prayer in travel; we do not find it in the Book of Allah, we find mention of the prayer of residence. Umayyah said: Abdullah ibn Umar said: O son of my brother, indeed Allah sent to us Muhammad while we knew nothing, and we only do what we saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. And shortening prayer in travel is a sunnah which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established."
"4874","221 - Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Shiri informed us, in Naysabur: Ismail ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Bakr al-Qari informed them: Abd al-Ghafir ibn Muhammad al-Farisi informed us: Abu Sahl Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfaraayini informed us: Dawud ibn al-Husayn ibn Uqayl al-Bayhaqi narrated: Yahya ibn Yahya al-Tamimi al-Naysaburi narrated: al-Layth ibn Sad informed us: from al-Zuhri: from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman: from Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid: that he said to Abdullah ibn Umar: We find the prayer of residence and the prayer of fear in the Quran, and we do not find the prayer of travel in the Quran. Ibn Umar said: Son of my brother, indeed Allah sent to us Muhammad while we knew nothing, so we only do as we saw Muhammad, upon him be peace, do. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ishaq ibn Isa from Layth from Ibn Shihab from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman. And al-Nasai narrated it from Yusuf ibn Said from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad from Abdullah al-Shuaythi from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham; al-Shuaythi said: Al-Zuhri used to narrate this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr. And from Qutaybah from al-Layth from Ibn Shihab from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rumh from al-Layth with this chain. And Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala from Shuayb ibn al-Layth from his father. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah from Yazid ibn Mawhab from al-Layth from Ibn Shihab from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr. And he narrated it with this chain and said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr."
"4875","Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani from Abdullah ibn Umar. 222 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to me: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: Humayd informed us: from Bakr ibn Abdullah: from Ibn Umar, and Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha at al-Batha, then slept a while, then entered Makkah. And Ibn Umar used to do it."
"4876","223 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated: Shurayh ibn al-Numan narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Ayyub: from Nafi: and from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani: from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha, then slept a while, then entered and circumambulated the House, meaning at al-Muhassab. Abu Dawud narrated it from Imam Ahmad from Musa from Hammad from Humayd. Humayd dropped from Shurayhs narration."
"4877","Another: 224 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, recited to him: Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us: Abu Said al-Simsar - he is Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Musa - informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah informed us: al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated: Sufyan ibn Habib narrated: Humayd al-Tawil narrated: from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani: from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enjoy this House, for it has been demolished twice and will be raised on the third. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdullah ibn Qahtabah from al-Hasan ibn Qazaah."
"4878","Another: 225 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated, he said: Humayd narrated: from Bakr: from Ibn Umar, who said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Makkah saying talbiyah for Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make it Umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall one of us go to Mina while his organ drips with semen? He said: Yes. Then the censers blazed at al-Batha. And Ali came from Yemen, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For what did you enter ihram? For with us is your sacrificial animal. He said: I entered ihram with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram. Humayd said: I informed the people of that while Tawus was sitting, and he said: Thus was the hadith."
"4879","226 - Abu Ahmad and Abu Tahir informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Rawh and Affan narrated, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd, Affan said in his hadith: Humayd informed us: from Bakr ibn Abdullah: from Ibn Umar: that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Makkah with his companions saying talbiyah - Affan said: saying tahlil - for Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes may make it Umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall one of us go to Mina while his organ drips with semen? He said: Yes. And the censers blazed, and Ali ibn Abi Talib came from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For what did you enter ihram? He said: I entered ihram with what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram. Rawh said: For with us is a sacrificial animal for you. Humayd said: I narrated it to Tawus, and he said: Thus did the people do. Affan said: Make it Umrah. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the narration of Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Jabir ibn Abdullah."
"4880","Bakr ibn Amr al-Naji Abu al-Siddiq from Abdullah ibn Umar. 227 - Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib al-Harbi informed us, there: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Hasan al-Qazzaz informed them: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya - he is Ibn Said - narrated: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad - he is Ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi - narrated, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to me: Hammam narrated: from Qatadah: from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji: from Abdullah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Shubah narrated it from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar as marfu. And more than one narrated it from Hammam as marfu."
"4881","228 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isbahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali narrated: Abu Khaythamah narrated: Abd al-Samad narrated: Hammam narrated: Qatadah narrated: from Abu al-Siddiq: from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the lahd, say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."
"4882","229 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Wahid - meaning al-Haddad - narrated: Hammam narrated: from Qatadah: from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji: from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah."
"4883","230 - With it my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us: from Qatadah: from Abu al-Siddiq: from Ibn Umar, likewise, except that he said: in the grave."
"4884","231 - With it my father narrated to me: Affan ibn Muslim narrated: from Hammam with its chain, and in it: and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4885","232 - With it my father narrated to me: Waki narrated: from Hammam with its chain similarly."
"4886","233 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated, they said: Hammam narrated: Qatadah narrated: from Abu al-Siddiq: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in their graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4887","234 - With it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz narrated: Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi narrated: Shubah narrated: from Qatadah: from Abu al-Siddiq: from Ibn Umar, who said: When you place the deceased in his grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun from Hammam. And Yazid said: None raised this hadith but Hammam. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Muhammad ibn Kathir from Hammam. And al-Nasai narrated it, in the book of the deeds of day and night, from Sulayman ibn Sayf from Said ibn Amir. And from Suwayd ibn Nasr from Ibn al-Mubarak from Shubah from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar as his saying. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili. And from Ibn Qahtabah from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid from Abu Dawud from Shubah as marfu. Al-Daraqutni said: Hammam narrated it from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Yazid ibn Harun, Said ibn Amir, Hajjaj ibn Minhal and Hudbah narrated it from him. And there was disagreement from Waki: Ahmad ibn Abi al-Raja narrated it from Waki from Hammam from Qatadah from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji from Ibn Umar, and he erred in it; and Surayh ibn Yunus and others opposed him and narrated it from Waki from Hammam from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq, and it is correct. And it is said: from Hisham al-Dastuwai from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and what is preserved from Hisham is mawquf, from the saying of Ibn Umar and his deed. And likewise Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Muadh ibn Hisham narrated it from Hisham. And likewise Shubah narrated it from Qatadah from Abu al-Siddiq from Ibn Umar as mawquf, and it is what is preserved."
"4888","Thawr, not attributed, from Ibn Umar. 235 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to me: Umar ibn Sulaym narrated, he used to live among Banu Qushayr, he said: Thawr narrated to me, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: What is the origin of this pebbling in the mosque? He said: We were rained upon at night. We came to the mosque for prayer, and a man would carry pebbles in his garment and cast them and pray upon them. In the morning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this? They told him, and he said: What a fine mat this is. He said: So the people adopted it. I said to him: What was the origin of this saffron? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came for Fajr prayer and there was phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped it and said: How ugly is this? He said: The man who spat came and scraped it, then daubed its place with saffron, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the place he said: This is better than that. I said: Why is it that when one of us relieves himself he looks at it when he rises from it? He said: The angel says to him: Look at what you were stingy with, what it has become. Thus Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated in the mention of pebbles from the narration of Umar ibn Sulaym from Abu al-Walid, whose name is Abdullah ibn al-Harith."
"4889","Jabalah ibn Suhaym al-Shaybani Abu Sarirah al-Kufi from Ibn Umar. 236 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn al-Tarrah informed us, in Baghdad: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf al-Urmawi informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nuqur informed us: Ali ibn Umar ibn Muhammad al-Harbi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Usayd al-Isbahani narrated, dictation: Yahya ibn Waqid Abu Salih al-Tai narrated: Yahya ibn Abi Ghunyah narrated: from his father: from Jabalah ibn Suhaym: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you visits his brother and sits with him, let him not rise until he seeks his permission."
"4890","Another: 237 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isbahan, and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr, in Cairo: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Khadir ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Marwazi narrated: Abu Muadh al-Nahwi al-Fadl ibn Khalid narrated: Abu Hamzah narrated: from Raqabah ibn Masqalah: from Jabalah ibn Suhaym: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever of you prays, let him not spread as the dog spreads his forearms. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Aishah. And in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Be balanced in prostration, and let none of you spread his arms as the dog spreads."
"4891","Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim al-Nawfali al-Madani from Ibn Umar. 238 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated: Ubadah ibn Muslim al-Fazari narrated: Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never omitted these words morning and evening: O Allah, I ask You for well-being in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my world, my family and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and secure my fears. O Allah, guard me from before me and behind me, from my right and my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being seized from beneath me. He said: Meaning collapse."
"4892","239 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Abu Nuaym narrated: Ubadah ibn Muslim narrated: Jubayr ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr narrated: that he was sitting with Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in his supplication evening and morning, he never omitted it until he parted the world and until he died: O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my world, my family and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and secure my fears. O Allah, guard me from before me and behind me, from my right and my left, and from above me, and I seek refuge in You from being seized from beneath me. Abu Dawud narrated it from Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi from Waki. And from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Ibn Numayr, both from Ubadah ibn Muslim. And al-Nasai narrated it, in the deeds of day and night, from Amr ibn Mansur from Abu Nuaym. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad from Waki. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from Fayyad ibn Zuhayr from Waki."
"4893","Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Himsi from Ibn Umar. 240 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated: Ibn Thawban informed us: from his father: from Makhul: from Jubayr ibn Nufayr: from Abdullah ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he does not gargle."
"4894","241 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated. Al-Tabarani said: And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated: from his father: from Makhul: from Jubayr ibn Nufayr: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah, Exalted, accepts repentance from the servant so long as he does not gargle."
"4895","242 - Abu Jafar informed us, also: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abdullah, known as Sammawayh, informed us: Asim ibn Ali narrated. And Ali ibn Ayyash narrated, they said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated: from his father: from Makhul: from Jubayr ibn Nufayr: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he does not gargle."
"4896","243 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit informed us: my father narrated to me: from Makhul: from Jubayr ibn Nufayr: from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he does not gargle."
"4897","244 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us, in Isbahan: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr al-Salhani informed them, recited to him. And Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, by ijazah: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us. And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us: Mahmud al-Sayrafi informed them, while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, they said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated: Uthman ibn Said narrated: Ibn Thawban narrated: from his father: from Makhul: from Jubayr ibn Nufayr: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Indeed Allah, Exalted, accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he does not gargle. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Ali ibn Ayyash and Isam ibn Khalid from Ibn Thawban. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub from Ali ibn Ayyash. And from Ibn Bashshar from Abu Amir al-Aqadi from Abd al-Rahman, and said: A good, strange hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Rashid ibn Sad al-Ramli from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Ibn Thawban. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili. Al-Daraqutni said: It was narrated from Musa ibn Dawud from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban from Makhul from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Ibn Umar. And what is correct is Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban from his father from Makhul; thus Ali ibn al-Jad and others narrated it."
"4898","Another: 245 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him: Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mihrabazd informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated: Ibn Wahb narrated: Muawiyah - he is Ibn Salih - narrated to me: from al-Harith: from Zayd ibn Artah: from Jubayr ibn Nufayr: that Abdullah ibn Umar saw a youth praying, having lengthened his prayer and been verbose in it, and said: Who knows this one? A man said: I do. Abdullah ibn Umar said: If I knew him I would command him to lengthen bowing and prostration, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the servant stands praying, his sins are brought and placed upon his head or his shoulder, and whenever he bows or prostrates they fall from him."
"4899","246 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated, and he mentioned with its chain likewise. Except that he said: upon his head and his shoulder. Abdullah ibn Salih we brought out as a witness."
"4900","Habib ibn Abi Thabit, and his fathers name is Qays, ibn Dinar al-Asadi Abu Yahya al-Kufi from Ibn Umar. 247 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Razzaq narrated: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Ata informed me: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar: that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. [The matn breaks off in the source row; the chain ends here.]"
"4901","248 - Abu Jafar Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated: Abd al-Razzaq narrated: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Ata informed me: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqba and no umra; whoever is given something as umra or ruqba, it is his for his life and his death. The wording is one, and in al-Dabaris narration he added, he said: Ruqba is to say: this is for the last of me and you in death, and umra is to make it his for his life by giving it for their lives."
"4902","249 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated: from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not give as ruqba; whoever is given something as ruqba it is his, and do not give as umra; whoever is given something as umra it is in the path of inheritance. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, and Ibn Majah narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur, both from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Nasai narrated it also from Abdullah ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Bakr from Ibn Jurayj, and from Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim from Waki from Yazid ibn Ziyad. Al-Daraqutni said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrates it from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Ibn Umar as marfu, and Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad narrated it from Habib from Ibn Umar as marfu about ruqba without umra, and Misar narrated from Habib about umra without ruqba as marfu also, and it was narrated from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Amr ibn Dinar, and Kamil Abu al-Ala from Habib as marfu, and the mawquf is more likely."
"4903","Another: 250 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not prevent women from going out to the mosques, and their houses are better for them."
"4904","251 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not prevent women from the mosques, and their houses are better for them."
"4905","252 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid informed us: from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent women from the mosques, and their houses are better for them. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Yazid ibn Harun from al-Awwam. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah from Yazid ibn Harun. We only intended from the hadith: and their houses are better for them; for his saying: do not prevent women from the mosques, it has been mentioned in the Sahih."
"4906","Another: 253 - Imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli, and Abu al-Fath Masud ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Jundani, and Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani, and Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us, in Isbahan, and Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad al-Thaqafi, in Damascus: Umm Ibrahim Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Muaddib Abu al-Shamqamqaq narrated, at Qasr Ibn Hubayrah: Hamid ibn Yahya al-Balkhi narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Suayr ibn al-Khums: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Sad is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah is in Paradise. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Habib from Ibn Umar but Suayr, nor from Suayr but Sufyan; Hamid is alone in it."
"4907","254 - Abu al-Qasim Zinki ibn Abi al-Wafa ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Bihimi informed us, in Marw: Abdullah Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Sayyar al-Dahhan informed them, recited to him: Abu Sahl Najib ibn Maymun ibn Sahl al-Wasiti informed us: Abu al-Fadl Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sharii al-Khwarizmi informed us, dictation, he came to us in Herat from Jurjan as a messenger: Abu Bakr al-Shafii - he is Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim - informed us: Junayd ibn Hakim narrated: Hamid ibn Yahya narrated: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated: from Suayr ibn al-Khums: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman, and Ali, and Talhah, and al-Zubayr, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Said ibn Zayd, and Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was mentioned among the ten in this narration, and Sad was not mentioned. Junayd we mentioned for consideration."
"4908","Another: 255 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas and Ali ibn Sad al-Razi narrated, they said: Sahl ibn Zanjalah narrated: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated: from Harun ibn Antaarah: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I broke fast one day of Ramadan. He said: Without excuse or sickness? He said: Yes. He said: Evil is what you did. He said: Yes; what do you command me? He said: Free a slave. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I never owned a slave. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot. He said: Then feed sixty poor. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I do not fill my family. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket with dates in it. He said: Give it in charity. He said: To whom? He said: To the poorest you know. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, there is none between its two lava plains more needy than us. He said: Then feed your dependents. Harun ibn Antaarah: Abu Hatim ibn Hibban criticized him, and Imam Ahmad and Yahya ibn Main said of him: He is trustworthy. And Abu Zuraah al-Razi said: There is no harm in him, upright in hadith, and these imams know better than Ibn Hibban. Al-Daraqutni said: Harun ibn Antaarah narrated it from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Ibn Umar, and he erred in it. And what is correct is from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Talq ibn Habib from Said ibn al-Musayyib as mursal. And Mihran ibn Abi Umar said: from al-Thawri from Habib from al-Musayyib from Abu Hurayrah. And what is correct is mursal."
"4909","Another: 256 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated: Ahmad ibn Sahl ibn Ali al-Bahili narrated: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated: Hushaym narrated: from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, who said: A man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews killed my brother. He said: I shall surely give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; Allah will grant victory at his hand, and Allah will enable you over your brothers killer. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked up for that. So he sent for Ali and tied the banner for him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am bleary-eyed as you see, and he was bleary-eyed that day. So he spat in his eye. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I never suffered eye inflammation after that day. And he went forth. Abu Sufyan, his name is Said ibn Yahya al-Himyari al-Wasiti: Abu Zuraah said: truthful, and al-Daraqutni said: average, not strong."
"4910","Another: 257 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jili narrated, in Kufah: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to pledge to you for jihad. He said: Are your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: Then in them strive. It was narrated in the two Sahihs from the narration of Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from al-Saib ibn Farrukh from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As."
"4911","Another: 258 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Samad Maghammah narrated: al-Qasim ibn Dinar narrated: Ubayd Allah narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit: from Ibn Umar: that he was asked about the pregnant woman and the woman whose husband died, he said: We used to spend on them."
"4912","Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah al-Nahdi Abu Thawr al-Kufi from Ibn Umar. 259 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated: Zaidah narrated: Kulayb ibn Wail narrated: from Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah, kunya Abu Thawr, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and asked him, saying: What about Uthman, did he witness Badr? He said: No. Then the man left. A man said to Ibn Umar: This one will go and claim you criticized Uthman. He said: Did I do that? Bring the man to me. So he was brought back, and Ibn Umar said to him: Did you understand what I said to you? He said: Yes. He said: As for the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Uthman is in Your need and the need of Your Messenger, so he struck a share for him. And as for the day the two hosts met, Allah has pardoned him: Indeed those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met, the verse. And as for the pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the Confederates about the sacrificial animals, to make truce and peace with us, but they refused, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Uthman is in Your need and the need of Your Messenger, and I pledge for him, and he struck one of his hands upon the other. Go and strive your utmost. Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated it and added a man in its chain. Al-Bukhari narrated something like this hadith from the narration of Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Wahb from Ibn Umar."
"4913","260 - Hafiz Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja al-Hanbali informed us, in Isbahan: Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Yahya narrated: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated: Kulayb ibn Wail narrated: from Hani ibn Qays: from Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah al-Nahdi, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: O Abdullah ibn Umar, did Uthman witness the pledge of Ridwan? He said: No. He said: Did he witness Badr? He said: No. He said: Did he flee on the day the two hosts met? He said: Yes. The man left, and it was said to Ibn Umar: This one will return to his companions and tell them you attacked Uthman. He said: Did I do that? They said: So we say. He said: Bring the man back to me. So they brought him back, and he said: Did you memorize what I said to you? He said: Yes. I asked you about such and you said such, and I asked you about such and you said such. Ibn Umar said: As for the pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the people of Makkah to seek their permission to enter Makkah, but they refused, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and pledged for him and said: Uthman has gone in the need of Allah and the need of His Messenger, and I pledge for him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clapped one of his hands upon the other. And as for Badr, he said: Uthman is in the need of Allah and the need of His Messenger. So the Messenger of Allah struck a share for him and struck for none absent but him, then he recited this verse: Indeed those of you who turned back on the day the two hosts met, to the end of the verse. Then he said: Go now and strive your utmost."
"4914","261 - With it Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Musaddad narrated: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Kulayb ibn Wail: Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to me, he said: A man came to Ibn Umar, and he mentioned something similar. And in this narration is evidence that Kulayb ibn Wail heard it from Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah, and heard it from Hani ibn Qays from him, so he used to narrate it by both paths. And Allah knows best. Abu Dawud narrated from it: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, meaning on the day of Badr, and said: Uthman has gone in the need of Allah and the need of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I pledge for him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a share for him and struck for none absent but him, from Mahbub ibn Musa from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari from Kulayb ibn Wail from Hani ibn Qays from Habib."
"4915","Al-Hurr ibn Sayyah al-Nakhai al-Kufi from Ibn Umar. 262 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Hajjaj narrated: Sharik narrated: from al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days of every month: Thursday at the beginning of the month, the Monday following it, and the Monday following it. Al-Nasai narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani from Said ibn Sulayman from Sharik similarly. And from Yusuf ibn Said from Hajjaj from Sharik abridged. And he said: There was disagreement over al-Hurr; it was narrated from him from Hunaydah ibn Khalid from Hafsah. And narrated from him from Hunaydah from his mother from Umm Salamah. And from him from his wife from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4916","Hariz or Abu Hariz from Ibn Umar. 263 - Abu Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali ibn al-Khurayf al-Nasri informed us, a Baghdadi: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Farra informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib informed us: al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lului informed us: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Sijistani narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Khallad al-Bahili narrated: Yahya narrated: from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hariz or Abu Hariz informed me - the doubt is from Yahya - that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Farrukh ask Ibn Umar, he said: We trade with peoples wealth, and one of us comes to Makkah and spends the night guarding the wealth. He said: As for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he spent the night at Mina and spent the day there. Thus Abu Dawud brought it out in his Sunan."
"4917","Al-Hasan ibn Hadiyah from Ibn Umar. 264 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us. And Ishaq ibn Isa from Jarir ibn Hazim. 265 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: my grandfather Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid narrated, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us: from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit: from al-Hasan ibn Hadiyah, who said: I met Ibn Umar, and he said to me: From whom are you? I said: From the people of Oman. He said: From the people of Oman? I said: Yes. He said: Shall I not narrate to you what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I know a land called Oman, beside it - and Ishaq said: in its vicinity - is the sea; a Hajj from it is better than two Hajjs from other than it. The wording is Imam Ahmads narration. And in Ahmad ibn Manis narration: I said: From the people of Oman. He said: Shall I not narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say the like, and with him: beside it is the sea."
"4918","Al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan - his fathers name is Yasar - al-Basri Abu Said from Ibn Umar. 266 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us: Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah informed us: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated: Hammad narrated: from Yunus: from al-Hasan: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, He said: Whichever servant of My servants goes out striving in My path seeking My pleasure, if I return him I return him with what he attained of reward and spoil, and if I take him I forgive him and have mercy on him and admit him to Paradise."
"4919","267 - Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Rawh narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Yunus: from al-Hasan: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord, Exalted, that He said: Whichever servant of My servants goes out striving in My path seeking My pleasure, I guarantee to return him with what he attained of reward and spoil, and if I take him, to forgive him and have mercy on him and admit him to Paradise. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub from al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal similarly."
"4920","268 - Abu Jafar Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated: Asim ibn Ali narrated: my father Ali ibn Asim narrated: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated: from al-Hasan: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant swallows a draught better than a draught of anger he swallows seeking the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Yunus ibn Ubayd."
"4921","269 - My maternal uncle Imam, scholar, Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu Zuraah Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed them: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed us: al-Qasim al-Khatib informed us: Ali ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated: Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated: Bishr ibn Umar narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Yunus ibn Ubayd: from al-Hasan: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no draught greater in reward with Allah than a draught of anger a servant swallows seeking the Face of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Ali ibn Asim we brought out for support. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Shihab al-Hannat and Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated it from Yunus from al-Hasan from Ibn Umar as mawquf, and Ali ibn Asim raised it from Yunus, and the mawquf is more correct. I say: Hammad ibn Salamah raised it from Yunus."
"4922","Husayn ibn al-Harith al-Jadali Abu al-Qasim al-Kufi from Ibn Umar. 270 - Abu Jafar and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati informed us: Said ibn Sulayman narrated: from Abbad ibn al-Awwam: Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated: Husayn ibn al-Harith al-Jadali - Jadilah Qays - narrated, he said: The amir of Makkah addressed us and adjured the people, saying: Who saw the crescent on such-and-such day? Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon us to sacrifice upon sighting; if we do not see it and two just witnesses testify, we sacrifice upon their testimony. So I asked al-Husayn: Who is the amir of Makkah? He said: He is al-Harith ibn Hatib, brother of Muhammad ibn Hatib. Then the amir said: Among you is one more knowledgeable of Allah and His Messenger than I, and he witnessed this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gestured with his hand toward the man. Al-Husayn said: I said to an old man beside me: Who is this to whom the amir gestured? He said: He is Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he is more knowledgeable of Allah and His Messenger than he. So we went to Ibn Umar, and he said: Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command us. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim from Said ibn Sulayman."
"4923","Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar from his father. 271 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us: from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman: from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar: from his father, who said: I had a wife I loved, and Umar disliked her and commanded me to divorce her, but I refused. So he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah ibn Umar has a wife whom I dislike for him, and I commanded him to divorce her but he refused. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abdullah, divorce your wife. So I divorced her."
"4924","272 - With it my father narrated to me: Yahya narrated: from Ibn Abi Dhib: from his maternal uncle al-Harith: from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar: from his father, who said: I had a wife, and Umar disliked her. He said: Divorce her. I refused. So Umar went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Obey your father."
"4925","273 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated: from al-Harith: from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar: from his father, who said: I had a wife I loved and my father disliked her. He said to me: Divorce her. I refused. So he went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that. He said: Divorce her. So I divorced her."
"4926","274 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad: his father informed them, recited to him: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarifini informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us: Abdullah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated: Ali - he is Ibn al-Jad - narrated: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us: from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman: from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar: from his father, who said: I had a wife I loved and my father disliked her, so he commanded me to divorce her but I refused. Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah, divorce her. Abdullah ibn Wahb and Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated it from Ibn Abi Dhib. And Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Abd al-Malik ibn Amr from Ibn Abi Dhib. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad from Yahya ibn Said. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Ibn al-Mubarak from Ibn Abi Dhib, and said: A good, sound hadith; we know it only from the hadith of Ibn Abi Dhib. And al-Nasai narrated it from Ismail ibn Masud from Khalid ibn al-Harith from Ibn Abi Dhib. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar from Yahya ibn Said, and Uthman ibn Umar from Ibn Abi Dhib. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan from al-Muqaddami from Yahya al-Qattan, and Umar ibn Ali from Ibn Abi Dhib."
"4927","Hayyan ibn Iyas al-Bariqi al-Wasiti from Abdullah ibn Umar. 275 - Abu Jafar Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yusuf al-Qadi narrated: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated. Al-Tabarani said: And Musa ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated, they said: Shubah narrated: from Hayyan al-Bariqi, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Two rakahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are lighter than one rakah of your prayer."
"4928","276 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad: his father informed them, recited to him, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Hababah informed us: Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - informed us: Ali narrated: Shubah informed us: from Hayyan al-Azdi, who said: I heard Ibn Umar; a man said to him: Our imam lengthens the prayer. He said: Two rakahs of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were lighter than one rakah of his prayer."
"4929","Khalid ibn Aslam, brother of Zayd, freedman of Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abdullah ibn Umar. 277 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us, in Isbahan: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated: Ahmad ibn Shabib narrated: my father narrated: from Yunus: from Ibn Shihab: from Khalid ibn Aslam, who said: We went out with Abdullah ibn Umar walking, and a bedouin caught up with us and said: Are you Abdullah ibn Umar? He said: Yes. He said: I asked about you and was directed to you. Tell me: Does the paternal aunt inherit? Ibn Umar said: I do not know. He said: You do not know and we do not know? He said: Yes; go to the scholars and ask them. When he turned away, he kissed his hands, then said: Excellent is what Abu Abd al-Rahman said; he is asked about what he does not know, so he says: I do not know. The bedouin said: The saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And those who hoard gold and silver. Ibn Umar said: Whoever hoards it and does not pay its zakah, woe to him; this was only before zakah was revealed; when it was revealed, Allah made it a purification. Then he turned to me and said: I would not care if I had the like of Uhud in gold, knowing its number, paying its zakah and acting in it in obedience to Allah. Al-Nasai brought it out from Amr ibn Sawwad from Ibn Wahb from Ibn Lahiah from Uqayl from Ibn Shihab similarly. And al-Bukhari narrated it as a comment, he said: Ahmad ibn Shabib said: my father narrated, in the mention of zakah."
"4930","Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi from Ibn Umar. 278 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, and Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad, in Naysabur: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us: al-Hakim Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hafiz informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Uthman al-Uthmani narrated, in Baghdad: Nasr - meaning Ibn Ali al-Jahdami - narrated: Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not beat slaves, for you do not know what you coincide with."
"4931","279 - Abu Jafar and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated: Khalid ibn Khidash narrated: Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated: from his father: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not beat the owned, for you do not know what you coincide with."
"4932","Dawud ibn Ismail al-Ansari from Ibn Umar. 280 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there: Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated: Shabbabah narrated: Asim ibn Suwayd narrated: Dawud ibn Ismail al-Ansari narrated to me: from Ibn Umar: that he attended a funeral at al-Awsat in the house of Sad ibn Ubadah, and came walking to Banu Amr ibn Awf at the courtyard of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. It was said to him: Where are you heading, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: I am heading to this mosque among Banu Amr ibn Awf; for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays in it, it is as the equal of an Umrah."
"4933","Rashid al-Himmani Abu Muhammad from Ibn Umar. 281 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated. Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated, they said: Ghassan ibn Burzin narrated: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to me: from Ibn Umar, who said: You saw us, and none of us deemed himself more entitled to his dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother; then the dinar and dirham became dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When people are miserly with the dinar and dirham, and follow the tails of cattle, and abandon jihad, Allah will impose upon them humiliation which He will not remove from them until they return to their affair."
"4934","Razin ibn Sulayman al-Ahmari from Ibn Umar. 282 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us, in Damascus: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Mawazini al-Sulami informed them, it was said to him: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd ibn Sadan al-Shahid informed you, in Damascus: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Rabi informed us: Abu al-Abbas Hajib ibn Arkin al-Farghani informed us, in what I read to him: Muhammad ibn Jabir al-Muharibi narrated: Yahya - he is Ibn Yala - narrated: from his father: from Ghaylan ibn Jami: from Alqamah ibn Marthad: from Razin ibn Sulayman al-Ahmari: that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar; a man asked him about a man who had a wife and divorced her thrice so she became separated from him, then another married her after him and closed the door upon her, let down the curtain, and set down the saddle-bags, then divorced her: is she lawful for her husband? Ibn Umar said: I was sitting by this pillar with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon this pulpit when a man came to him and asked him about the like of this, and he said: No, until he tastes the sweetness."
"4935","283 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us, in Isbahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated: al-Thawri narrated: from Alqamah ibn Marthad: from Razin al-Ahmari - or Ibn Razin al-Ahmari, Bishr doubted - from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorced his wife thrice, then a man married her and divorced her before consummating with her. He said: She is not lawful for the first until he tastes her sweetness."
"4936","284 - Abu Ahmad al-Harbi and Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Alqamah ibn Marthad: from Razin ibn Sulayman al-Ahmari: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorces his wife thrice, then another marries her and closes the door and lets down the curtain, then divorces her before consummating with her: is she lawful for the first? He said: No, until he tastes the sweetness. Al-Nasai narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan from Waki."
"4937","Zadhan al-Kindi, their freedman, Abu Umar, and it is said Abu Abdullah, al-Kufi al-Bazzaz from Ibn Umar. 285 - Abu Jafar Muhammad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated: Abu al-Ahwas narrated: from Ata ibn al-Saib: from Zadhan: from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is prompted with: there is no god but Allah, at his death, will enter Paradise. Al-Daraqutni said: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu al-Nadr narrated it from Ata ibn al-Saib from Zadhan from Umar. And Hammad said: from Salamah from Ata from Zadhan from one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Asbat ibn Muhammad said: from Ata ibn al-Saib from Zadhan as his saying. And al-Husayn ibn Salih said: from Ata from a man from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and did not mention Zadhan or other than him. And it is more likely. And Sulayman al-Taymi said: from Ata from Zadhan as mursal, and he mentioned other than that; and this is an error, because he changed at the end of his affair."
"4938","Al-Zubayr ibn al-Walid al-Shami from Ibn Umar. 286 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi informed us, there: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Samiri informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Abbas ibn Abdullah al-Tarqufi narrated: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated: Safwan ibn Amr narrated, he said: Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami narrated to me: that he heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Walid narrate from Abdullah ibn Umar. 287 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us. And Abu Jafar informed us, also: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, they said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated: Abu al-Mughirah narrated: Safwan ibn Amr narrated: from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami: that he heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Walid narrate from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided or traveled and night overtook him, he said: O earth, my Lord and your Lord is Allah; I seek refuge in Allah from your evil and the evil of what is in you, and the evil of what was created in you and the evil of what crawls upon you; I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of lion and black, snake and scorpion, and from the evil of the dweller of the land and from the evil of a parent and what it bore. The wording is one, except that in Abu Nuayms narration: crawls upon you. And in al-Tarqufis narration: from the evil of every lion and black. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu al-Mughirah, and in his narration: from the evil of every lion and black. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Amr ibn Uthman. And al-Nasai brought it out, in the book of the deeds of day and night, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, both from Baqiyyah from Safwan."
"4939","Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah al-Thaqafi al-Basri from Ibn Umar. 288 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Razzaq ibn Nasr ibn al-Muslim al-Najjar al-Dimashqi informed us, there: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi al-Ala informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Uthman ibn Abdullah al-Azdi informed us, in Damascus: Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Khurshidh informed us, his saying: Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Marwazi informed us: Ibrahim ibn Rashid narrated: Muslim narrated. 289 - And Abu al-Muzaffar Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Munim ibn Mashadhah informed us, in Shahrastan: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, recited to him: Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Sabuni informed us: Abu Said Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Razi informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Yahya ibn Durays al-Razi informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated. 290 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad and Fatimah bint Sad al-Khayr informed us: Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated. 291 - And my maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed them, recited to him in Baghdad: al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Bakhtari informed us: Ahmad - he is Ibn Ishaq ibn Salih - narrated: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated: Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated: from Ziyad ibn Jubayr: from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling animal for animal on credit. The wording is one, except that in Ibrahim ibn Rashids narration: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade. Muhammad ibn Dinar Abu Bakr al-Taji al-Basri: Yahya ibn Main said: weak, and Abu Ahmad ibn Adi said: good in hadith."
"4940","Ziyad ibn Subayh al-Hanafi al-Makki, and it is said al-Basri, from Ibn Umar. 292 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated. 293 - And Abu Tahir al-Harimi and Abu Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibah Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: Said ibn Ziyad al-Shaybani informed us: Ziyad ibn Subayh al-Hanafi narrated, he said: I was standing praying toward the House with an old man beside me, and I lengthened the prayer and placed my hands upon my waist, so the old man struck my chest a blow unsparingly. I said to myself: What has disturbed him about me? So I hastened to finish. There was a boy behind him. I said: Who is this, O old man? He said: This is Abdullah ibn Umar. So I sat until he finished, and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what has disturbed you about me? He said: Are you he? I said: Yes. He said: That is bracing oneself in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid it. Their wording is one, except that in Imam Ahmads narration: and an old man beside me, and with him: I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman. Imam Ahmad narrated it also from Waki from Said ibn Ziyad and similarly. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Hannad from Waki. And al-Nasai narrated it from Humayd ibn Masadah from Sufyan ibn Habib from Said ibn Ziyad similarly."
"4941","Ziyad ibn Fayruz al-Basri Abu al-Aliyah al-Barra from Ibn Umar. 294 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi informed us, there: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Qubays al-Ghassani informed them, recited to him: Abu Nasr al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tallab informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Yahya al-Sharani informed us, he came to us: Muhammad ibn Khalaf - he is al-Asqalani Abu Nasr - narrated: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Ayyub: from Abu al-Aliyah, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: Do you count killing as anything, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands the owner of arrows who bared their heads to hold them by their heads, lest he scratch a Muslim or tear his clothes. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn Abdullah. And from the hadith of Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa from his father."
"4942","Zayd ibn Aslam, freedman of Umar, from Abdullah ibn Umar. 295 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khatib informed us: al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar informed us: Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated: Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa narrated: my father narrated: Hisham ibn Sad narrated: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated: that Abdullah ibn Umar entered upon Muawiyah, and he said: Your need, O Abu Abd al-Rahman! He said: The grants of the freedmen, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the first thing that came to him, begin with the freedmen. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan."
"4943","Another: 296 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq informed us, in his book, and my maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us from him, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us: Hafiz Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us: Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Atiq narrated: Mutarrif narrated: Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated: from his father: from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made lawful for us of blood are two bloods and of dead meat are two dead: of dead meat, the fish and the locust; and of blood, the liver and the spleen. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Musab from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd from his father. And thus al-Daraqutni brought it out in his book. And from al-Husayn ibn Ismail from Ali ibn Muslim from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from his father. Abdullah ibn Zayd was weakened by some and declared trustworthy by some."
"4944","Another: 297 - Abu Muhammad Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Katib informed us, in Baghdad: Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Allanah informed us, by ijazah: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya - he is Ibn Said - narrated: Humayd ibn al-Rabi ibn Humayd ibn Malik al-Lakhmi narrated: Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated: Hisham ibn Sad narrated: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from the beast while it is alive is dead meat."
"4945","298 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed them: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir informed us: Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Qattan informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated: Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated: Man ibn Isa narrated: from Hisham ibn Sad: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever is cut from a beast while it is alive, what is cut of it is dead meat. Thus Ibn Majah brought it out. And al-Daraqutni narrated it from Muhammad ibn Makhlad from Humayd ibn al-Rabi. I say: Humayd we brought out as a witness. Al-Daraqutni mentioned the disagreement in it, then said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn Umar as mawquf, and the mawquf from Ibn Umar is more correct."
"4946","Another: 299 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed me: from Zayd ibn Aslam: that he informed him that he used to see Ibn Umar with the button of his shirt undone, so Ibn Umar was asked about that and said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Hajib ibn Arkin from Abu al-Walid Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bakkar al-Qurashi."
"4947","Another: 300 - Imam Abu Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Ibrahim al-Harbi al-Waiz informed us, in al-Mawsil: Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Rahabi informed them: al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi informed us: Qadi Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated, dictation: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated: Yahya - he is Ibn Hassan - narrated: Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated: from his father, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Throw dust in the faces of the praisers."
"4948","301 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Khushui informed us: Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khidr al-Sulami informed them: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kinani informed us: Tammam ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Razi informed us: Khaythamah ibn Sulayman narrated, from his wording: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad informed us: my father informed us: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated. 302 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Tai narrated: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad al-Bayruti narrated, he said: my father informed me: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Throw dust in the faces of the praisers. Khaythamah did not say: that he. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salm from Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Dhakwan al-Dimashqi from Marwan ibn Muhammad from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad from Zayd ibn Aslam. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of al-Miqdad. Al-Daraqutni said: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated it from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam ibn Zayd from Ibn Umar. And al-Darawardi opposed them and narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam as mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Hashim ibn Sad and Hafs ibn Maysarah opposed them and narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam from Jami ibn Abi Rashid as mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4949","Another: 303 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, in Isbahan: Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Rifah Umarah ibn Wathimah ibn Musa ibn al-Furat al-Misri narrated: Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wives of the people of Paradise sing to their husbands with the finest voices anyone ever heard. Of what they sing: and of what they sing: Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam but Muhammad. Ibn Abi Maryam is alone in it."
"4950","Another: 304 - With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Hatim ibn Muhammad ibn Humayd Abu Adi al-Baghdadi narrated: Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated: Asim ibn Yusuf al-Yarbui narrated: Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a piece of gold, the first charity of a mine that came to him, and he said: What is this? They said: Charity from a mine of ours. He said: There will be mines, and in them will be the worst of Allahs creation, Mighty and Majestic. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Suayr but Asim ibn Yusuf."
"4951","305 - Abu Tammam Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Husayn, known, informed us, in Isbahan: his maternal grandfather Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Musa informed them, recited to him: Qadi Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: my fathers uncle Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Muaddal informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Zayd al-Muaddal narrated: Imran ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated: Asim ibn Yusuf al-Kufi narrated: Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a piece of gold from mines, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be mines, and in them will be the worst of Allahs creation, Mighty and Majestic."
"4952","Another: 306 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, in Baghdad: Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them: Abu al-Ghanayim Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sawwaq al-Bundar informed us: Abu al-Faraj Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muslimah informed us, dictation: Abu Muhammad Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ismail informed us: al-Qasim ibn Zakariya Abu Bakr al-Muqri narrated: Suwayd ibn Said narrated: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to me: from Zayd ibn Aslam: from Ibn Umar: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Only he who hopes for it enters Paradise, and only he who fears it is kept from the Fire, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, only has mercy on him who shows mercy. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the narration of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Usamah ibn Zayd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah only has mercy on the merciful among His servants."
"4953","Another: 307 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, recited to him: Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Aqil al-Qattan informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us: Abu al-Azhar Ahmad ibn al-Azhar informed us: Jafar ibn Awn narrated: Hisham ibn Sad narrated: from Zayd ibn Aslam, and Nafi: from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion is sincere advice. We said: To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: To Allah and His Messenger and the leaders of the Muslims and their commons. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Tamim ibn Aws al-Dari. Its end, and praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant abundant peace."
